 "root_cause": "Metadata-less frame extraction enumerated the decoder before checking the count, consuming one extra frame and exposing valid requested frames to an irrelevant damaged tail. Both metadata-less and target sampling also left retained decode iterators without explicit close.",
 "changes": [
  "Consume at most the requested decode count with islice in the metadata-less fallback; preserve partial valid output on EOF",
  "Share an optional-close decode context between target sampling and fallback, closing before the next seek or container exit",
  "Close on normal completion, early stop, timestamp/decode/image errors; preserve original exception context when close fails",
  "Keep plain non-close iterators injectable and leave failed seek behavior unchanged",
  "Preserve nearest real timestamp selection, frame/image/output budgets, processing timeouts and actual subprocess ownership"
 ],
